// # Fleettick Cutover Checklist — Pre-Flip Verification
//
// Logline: Ordered checklist a manager verifies before flipping
//          management ticks from the shell fleet-tick.sh/autosnap.sh
//          automation to the pure .oo fleettick timer (RFC-0013).
//
// Setup:   Units + runbook ship under buildbox/fleettick/deploy/ and
//          docs/fleettick-runbook.oot. Soak evidence:
//          docs/audit-history/2026-11-06-fleettick-soak.oot.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Artifact parity.
//   2. Live-behavior checks.
//   3. Environment + scheduling checks.
//   4. Flip sequencing and rollback.
//   5. Post-flip observation.

// ## 1. Artifact parity

// 1.1 Binary parity — sha256sum of ~/.local/bin/fleettick equals a
//     fresh oodac.real build of sweep_main.oo at the pinned commit
//     (binary-parity law).
// 1.2 Manual tick — run the installed binary by hand under the gate
//     env; expect TICK_LOCK took, all 12 sections, TICK done, exit 0.

// ## 2. Live-behavior checks

// 2.1 Shell parity — diff .fleet-state.txt against the last
//     fleet-tick.sh output: repo set, verdict classes, alert
//     semantics match (pane-quota UNKNOWN is an accepted delta).
// 2.2 Lock proof — hold .fleet-tick/lock fresh: invoker prints
//     TICK_LOCK held + TICK SKIP, exit 0. Remove: next run took.
// 2.3 Alert path — if a real breach exists at flip time, confirm the
//     ALERT-* spool file lands and clears on recovery.

// ## 3. Environment + scheduling checks

// 3.1 Unit env — timer's Environment= carries OODA_NO_JAIL=1,
//     OO_LIST_AMBIENT_QUOTA, OODA_FLEET_HOME, OODA_FLEET_XDG.
//     A jailed unit emits ERR verdicts (runtime-env.oot).
// 3.2 Overlap — OnUnitActiveSec counts from service completion; a
//     manual `start` during a live tick must print held/SKIP.
// 3.3 Cron fallback — if cron is used instead, the fragment derives
//     OODA_FLEET_XDG via $(id -u); cron has no XDG_RUNTIME_DIR.

// ## 4. Flip sequencing and rollback

// 4.1 Old automation off first — fleet-tick.sh and autosnap.sh crons
//     removed or commented BEFORE enabling the timer. Never both.
// 4.2 Rollback kept — scripts stay on disk; rollback is
//     `systemctl --user stop fleettick.timer` + restore old cron line.
// 4.3 Flip = operator action — units ship inert by design.

// ## 5. Post-flip observation

// 5.1 First 3 ticks — journalctl shows took/sections/done each time,
//     alerts=0, state doc stable modulo live gauges (soak pattern).
// 5.2 First breach — watch the first genuine alert fire and clear;
//     spool logic is unit-tested but unobserved live.
// 5.3 First recovery — after any host/network blip, confirm
//     GATE-SKIP/ERR verdicts appear rather than silent skips.
